1
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Sometimes silence is the deadliest sound.

2
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Silence is a drama, history film directed by Martin Scorsese.

3
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
In the 17th century, two Portuguese Jesuit priests travel to Japan in an attempt to locate their
mentor, who is rumored to have committed apostasy, and to propagate Catholicism.

4
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Rodrigues, played by Andrew Garfield.

5
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Garupe, played by Adam Driver.

6
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Ferreira, played by Liam Neeson.

7
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Interpreter, played by Tadanobu Asano.

8
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Father Valignano, played by Ciarán Hinds.

9
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Old Samurai / Inoue, played by Issey Ogata.

10
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Silence is a 2016 epic historical drama film directed by Martin Scorsese from a screenplay by Jay Cocks and Scorsese,
based on the 1966 novel of the same name by Shūsaku Endō, marking the third filmed adaptation of the novel.

11
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The film stars Andrew Garfield, Adam Driver, Tadanobu
Asano, Ciarán Hinds and Liam Neeson.

12
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The plot follows two 17th-century Jesuit priests who travel from Portugal to Edo period Japan
via Macau to locate their missing mentor and spread Catholic Christianity.

13
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
It is the third of Scorsese's films about religious figures struggling with challenges of
faith, following The Last Temptation of Christ (1988) and Kundun (1997).

14
01:38:00,000 --> 01:38:06,000
The pre-production phase of the filmmaking for Silence went through a
cycle of over two decades of setbacks and reassessments.

15
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
After filming of The Wolf of Wall Street concluded in January 2013,
Scorsese committed to following it up with Silence.

16
01:52:00,000 --> 01:52:06,000
On April 19, 2013, Scorsese indicated that he would
begin production on Silence in 2014.

17
01:59:00,000 --> 01:59:06,000
Irwin Winkler was then announced as a producer, as were Randall Emmett and George Furla,
who would provide financing through their company Emmett/Furla Films.

18
02:06:00,000 --> 02:06:06,000
Soon thereafter, planning was made for the film to be shot in Taiwan.

19
02:13:00,000 --> 02:13:06,000
A long-time passion project for Scorsese, which he had developed for over 25 years, Silence premiered in
Rome on November 29, 2016, and was released in the United States on December 23, 2016.

20
02:20:00,000 --> 02:20:06,000
Though it received critical acclaim, being selected as one of the top ten films of the year by both the National Board of Review and the American Film Institute
and being nominated for the Academy Award for Best Cinematography, it was a box office bomb, grossing $24 million against its $50 million budget.

21
02:27:00,000 --> 02:27:06,000
The film explores themes of japan, based on novel or
book, christianity, missionary, remake.

22
02:34:00,000 --> 02:34:06,000
The tone is emotional.
